Ownership Duration: They must have been the official owner of the car in their previous country (e.g., the Netherlands) for at least 6 consecutive months before the date they moved to Portugal.
Previous Residency: They must prove they legally lived outside of Portugal for at least 6 consecutive months before moving.
The 12-Month Window: The application for the tax exemption must be submitted online to customs via a Declaração Aduaneira de Veículos (DAV) within 12 months of officially moving to Portugal.
Taxes Already Paid: They must prove that standard VAT and registration taxes were fully paid in the country of origin and were not refunded when leaving.
The 12-Month Lock: Once granted the free plates, the owner cannot sell, rent, or even lend the car to anyone else for the first 12 months. Doing so triggers an immediate fine and forces payment of the full tax. 

