Why People Get Caught and Fined
The Alfândega routinely impounds foreign-registered cars because many expats misunderstand the deadlines or the definition of "residency." Common pitfalls include:
The 20-Day Trap: If a person does not qualify for the "free" relocation exemption, they only have 20 working days from the moment the car physically enters Portugal to start the official, paid import process.
Becoming a Resident First: The moment an individual gets a Portuguese residency document or signs a rental contract, the clock starts ticking. If they continue to drive a Dutch or Spanish-plated car for months without starting the import or exemption paperwork, it is legally considered tax evasion, resulting in customs seizing the car and physical license. 

