However, because the car is currently impounded due to a customs fine, you cannot simply drive it away until the legal status is resolved. Your options depend entirely on whether you want to finish putting it on Portuguese plates first, or skip Portugal completely and take it to Spain.
Here are your three current legal options to get your car moving on paper:
Option 1: Pay the Fine, Finalize the DAV, and Get the Portuguese Plates
If you want the car on Portuguese plates before moving, you must resolve the impoundment first.
The Process: You must pay the pending Alfândega fine to get the car released from the impound lot. Because you have already submitted a DAV, you will need to pay any residual ISV tax or prove you meet the relocation exemption requirements. Once the taxes and fines are cleared, the IMT (Institute for Mobility and Transport) will issue Portuguese plates and your new registration document (Documento Único Automóvel - DUA).
The Downside: This will take time and money. If you get Portuguese plates, you will then have to repeat the entire export/import bureaucracy all over again when you register it in Spain a few weeks later.
Option 2: Convert the DAV into an "Export Transit" (Recommended)
Since your goal is to move to Spain immediately, you can negotiate with the Alfândega to let you take the car out of the country without fully registering it in Portugal.
The Process: You pay the customs fine for the past infraction to release the vehicle. Instead of finishing the Portuguese registration, you ask the Alfândega to process your DAV strictly as a Permanent Export / Transit.
How it works: Portugal can issue you temporary transit plates (plates with a yellow or red strip on the side) or allow you to transport the car out of Portugal on a flatbed tow truck directly to Spain. This cancels the need to pay full Portuguese registration taxes, as you are legally proving the car is leaving the Portuguese tax system.
Option 3: Leave the Car, Settle the Fine, and Transport It Directly to Spain
You do not need to wait in Portugal for the paperwork to clear if you use a professional transit company.
The Process: You can move to Spain now to start your new job and residency. You can authorize a legal representative (a Despachante Oficial or a lawyer) or a professional car transport company to handle the Alfândega payment and collect the car for you once it is released.
How it works: The transport company will load your car onto a trailer and haul it across the border to Spain. Since the car is moving on a trailer and not driving on Portuguese roads, it does not need active Portuguese plates to cross the border.
Your Next Step
Go to the Alfândega office handling your case (or log into the Portal das Finanças to check your DAV status) and ask them for the exact breakdown of the fine and release conditions for export.
